
//
//   This is a single-, double-, triple-, and quadruple-click detector
//   component for LinuxCNC.
//
//   Test copy of src/hal/components/multiclick.comp with the state machine
//   rewritten as an fsm block.  It validates the fsm implementation:
//   tests/multiclick-fsm runs it on the inputs and expected output of
//   tests/multiclick, where it matches the original cycle for cycle.  The
//   shipped component stays unchanged.
//
//   Outside those inputs it differs from the original in four ways:
//   - a timeout that is an exact multiple of the period fires one period
//     earlier: the fsm fires at timer >= timeout, the original at
//     timer > timeout (the defaults, 250 ms at 1 ms, are such multiples);
//   - the first run only enters IDLE, so a press already there in the
//     first cycle is acted on one cycle later;
//   - the function is not nofp, since timeouts are floating point;
//   - the timeouts are read from the params every cycle; the original
//     fixes them when it enters a state.
//
//   Copyright 2012 Sebastian Kuzminsky <seb@highlab.com>
